To determine how many more kilometers Bernice needs to drive, we first calculate her total driving distance so far:

\[
\text{Total Distance Driven} = 325 \text{ km/day} \times 4 \text{ days} = 1,\!300 \text{ km}
\]

Next, we subtract this distance from the total distance between San Diego and New York City:

\[
\text{Remaining Distance} = 1955 \text{ km} - 1,\!300 \text{ km} = 655 \text{ km}
\]

Therefore, Bernice will still need to drive **655** kilometers. 

\boxed{655}

